72
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:16,120
The parents of our troupe are not happy with our district

73
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:17,120
or council.

74
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:20,880
They feel we're kind of outsiders because two powerhouse troops

75
00:05:20,880 --> 00:05:25,160
in the area get more help from the district and council,

76
00:05:25,160 --> 00:05:28,080
because the district and council level volunteers

77
00:05:28,080 --> 00:05:31,920
are largely coming from those troops.

78
00:05:31,920 --> 00:05:35,840
This apparent nepotism contributes to the distrust

79
00:05:35,840 --> 00:05:38,640
of things that the council and the district do.

80
00:05:38,640 --> 00:05:40,520
I am interested in changing this

81
00:05:40,520 --> 00:05:42,800
and I wonder if you could tell me the benefits of working

82
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:44,600
with the district and the council.

83
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:46,560
Well, that's a really interesting question.

84
00:05:46,560 --> 00:05:48,600
And I will say this

85
00:05:48,600 --> 00:05:51,760
For my role as a scout master, because that's all I do,

86
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:55,680
That's the only thing I volunteer for is I'm a scout master,

87
00:05:55,680 --> 00:05:59,920
So district and council stuff kind of plays a relatively

88
00:05:59,920 --> 00:06:00,960
small role in that.

89
00:06:00,960 --> 00:06:05,440
I understand the support that we get from our scout district

90
00:06:05,440 --> 00:06:07,240
and our scout council,

91
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:10,960
But as far as the way that I have a relationship there,

92
00:06:10,960 --> 00:06:12,760
it's pretty minor.

93
00:06:12,760 --> 00:06:15,680
My focus is making scouting possible for my scouts

94
00:06:15,680 --> 00:06:18,640
and developing youth leaders and things like that.

95
00:06:18,640 --> 00:06:21,360
So the troop committee in my instance

96
00:06:21,360 --> 00:06:25,000
takes on the district and council relationships

97
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:27,360
From my standpoint. I'm being a little cynical,

98
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:30,560
but it seems to amount to a lot of frustratingly

99
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:31,920
over complicated paperwork.

100
00:06:31,920 --> 00:06:33,600
but I'm not a big paperwork guy

101
00:06:33,600 --> 00:06:35,360
if you haven't already figured that out,

102
00:06:35,360 --> 00:06:37,320
So take that with a green assault.

103
00:06:38,320 --> 00:06:41,280
I guess our highest profile interaction

104
00:06:41,280 --> 00:06:43,640
with our district and council

105
00:06:43,640 --> 00:06:46,000
is our summer camp,

106
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:48,760
because we attend our council summer camp every summer

107
00:06:48,760 --> 00:06:52,719
and getting eagle projects approved

108
00:06:52,719 --> 00:06:55,960
and eagle boards of review, that sort of thing.

109
00:06:55,960 --> 00:06:57,919
Now, years ago I was more involved

110
00:06:57,919 --> 00:07:00,159
at the district and nominally at the council level.

111
00:07:00,159 --> 00:07:03,560
I helped by planning and running some Weebelows weekends

112
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:05,479
And I believe, if I remember correctly,

113
00:07:05,479 --> 00:07:08,120
a camperee or two for our district.

114
00:07:08,120 --> 00:07:10,039
My wife and I ran an after-school

115
00:07:10,040 --> 00:07:12,720
Cub Scout program for a couple of years

116
00:07:12,720 --> 00:07:15,800
that had some council and district connections.

117
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:19,600
I worked at our summer camp on the camp staff

118
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:20,800
for about a dozen years,

119
00:07:20,800 --> 00:07:24,040
with a couple of those years being as the camp director.

120
00:07:24,040 --> 00:07:27,320
So I was an actual council employee.

121
00:07:28,320 --> 00:07:30,200
I've run training sessions.

122
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:32,160
I guess it's been a long time though

123
00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:34,240
It's been at least three or four or five years-

124
00:07:34,240 --> 00:07:36,160
since I've run a training session.

125
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:40,040
I think that our Scouts, outside

126
00:07:40,040 --> 00:07:42,560
of our participation in summer camp,

127
00:07:42,560 --> 00:07:44,600
I'm pretty sure they go to events

128
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:47,080
like a Marripad something or other.

129
00:07:48,280 --> 00:07:50,720
They haven't chosen to go to a camperee

130
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:55,080
or any kind of district event like that in a long time.

131
00:07:55,080 --> 00:07:58,040
We do have Scouts who are involved in the order of the arrow

132
00:07:58,040 --> 00:08:01,080
and that's probably the highest profile active program

133
00:08:01,080 --> 00:08:04,200
that our Scouts participate in above the troop level.

134
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:06,200
That just gives you a little bit of context

135
00:08:06,200 --> 00:08:07,200
for what I'm about to say,

136
00:08:07,200 --> 00:08:09,719
because I do know what you're talking about.

137
00:08:09,719 --> 00:08:11,800
when you mentioned that other troops

138
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:14,320
seemingly benefit from a closer connection

139
00:08:14,320 --> 00:08:16,000
with the district and the council,

140
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:18,960
I'm not exactly sure what advantages they would have.

141
00:08:18,960 --> 00:08:23,320
Maybe- I don't know- first in line at the banquet.

142
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:26,680
I don't think that there's really

143
00:08:26,680 --> 00:08:30,400
a giant advantage there. personally,

144
00:08:30,400 --> 00:08:32,159
because I've seen that in the past

145
00:08:32,159 --> 00:08:34,319
and as a younger man I might have been jealous

146
00:08:34,319 --> 00:08:36,919
of some of those associations and things like that.

147
00:08:36,919 --> 00:08:41,280
but now, having traveled the path for several miles,

148
00:08:41,280 --> 00:08:43,159
if you happen to have a troop

149
00:08:43,159 --> 00:08:46,439
with a lot of district or council volunteers

150
00:08:46,439 --> 00:08:49,199
involved with the troop, I guess that's nice.

151
00:08:49,199 --> 00:08:50,920
I don't see a lot of advantage in it

152
00:08:50,920 --> 00:08:53,400
and I certainly don't see anything unfair.

153
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:56,160
So I guess I would challenge that assumption

154
00:08:56,160 --> 00:08:58,480
because most of the time that perceived benefit

155
00:08:58,480 --> 00:08:59,839
really amounts to the fact

156
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:02,560
that you just have to have a number of adults

157
00:09:02,560 --> 00:09:03,680
involved with the given troop

158
00:09:03,680 --> 00:09:06,520
filling a district or council volunteer role

159
00:09:06,520 --> 00:09:09,440
and they end up having a whole higher profile

160
00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:10,800
at district or council events

161
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:13,800
and it could look like they benefit from them

162
00:09:13,800 --> 00:09:15,800
more than others. but I've never really

163
00:09:15,800 --> 00:09:17,440
found that to be the case.

164
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:19,920
So in the end, I'm probably not being much help

165
00:09:19,920 --> 00:09:23,840
with that- with your particular question-

166
00:09:23,840 --> 00:09:26,760
but I don't think I'm missing out on anything

167
00:09:27,760 --> 00:09:29,840
from the district or the council

168
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:31,920
and, more importantly, I don't think my scouts

169
00:09:31,920 --> 00:09:34,520
are missing out on anything either.

170
00:09:34,520 --> 00:09:37,960
We've had occasions where we've had district volunteers

171
00:09:37,960 --> 00:09:40,120
who are also adults involved with our troop

172
00:09:40,120 --> 00:09:43,080
and we've had council level volunteers

173
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:45,600
who are adults involved with our troop.

174
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:47,920
didn't seem to make a whole lot of difference

175
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:49,439
one way or the other.

176
00:09:49,439 --> 00:09:51,560
Now I'm not trying to actively discourage you

177
00:09:51,560 --> 00:09:53,600
from finding out what goes on at the district

178
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:56,319
or the council level. there's likely some good for you

179
00:09:56,360 --> 00:09:58,840
Personally, and maybe even your scouts,

180
00:09:58,840 --> 00:10:02,320
beyond the kind of administrative connection

181
00:10:02,320 --> 00:10:04,480
that you have to the district and the council.

182
00:10:04,480 --> 00:10:06,480
is there anything to be gained

183
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:08,120
that these other troops are getting

184
00:10:08,120 --> 00:10:09,760
that you're not. probably not,

185
00:10:09,760 --> 00:10:13,520
And I think this is a good opportunity for me to say this.

186
00:10:13,520 --> 00:10:16,120
I'm a one role kind of guy.

187
00:10:16,120 --> 00:10:20,600
There are a lot of people that wear many different hats.

188
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:23,360
maybe they're a unit level volunteer

189
00:10:23,360 --> 00:10:24,920
and a district level volunteer

190
00:10:24,920 --> 00:10:26,719
and a council level volunteer,

191
00:10:26,719 --> 00:10:30,199
and maybe they're involved in three things at each level.

192
00:10:30,199 --> 00:10:31,880
I'm not into that personally.

193
00:10:31,880 --> 00:10:36,880
Let's wear one hat, occupy one role and do it well.

194
00:10:37,160 --> 00:10:40,560
So, anyway, hope that helps with that particular question.

195
00:10:40,560 --> 00:10:43,719
I don't know if it did, but perhaps it does.

196
00:10:43,719 --> 00:10:46,880
Here's another email, again anonymous

197
00:10:46,880 --> 00:10:48,520
at the sender's request.

198
00:10:48,520 --> 00:10:51,520
I'm a new Wolf Den leader and a professional engineer.

199
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:53,400
I had completed wood badge

200
00:10:53,400 --> 00:10:56,040
and part of my ticket is incorporating STEM

201
00:10:56,040 --> 00:10:58,600
into Wolf Den leader training

202
00:10:58,600 --> 00:11:03,600
And STEM- S-T-E-M- an abbreviated way of saying

203
00:11:04,040 --> 00:11:07,439
science, technology, engineering and mathematics-

204
00:11:07,439 --> 00:11:08,959
and educational category

205
00:11:08,959 --> 00:11:11,079
that you hear a great deal about anymore.

206
00:11:11,079 --> 00:11:15,760
I- and the person asked this question goes on to say

207
00:11:15,760 --> 00:11:20,120
I also ran a successful STEM event for our Cubs,

208
00:11:20,120 --> 00:11:21,840
but at a district round table

209
00:11:21,840 --> 00:11:23,079
when I wanted to speak about it,

210
00:11:23,080 --> 00:11:26,240
I was told: well, that's Cub stuff, it's not for scouts,

211
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:29,600
so we'll have that done during the Cub presentation.

212
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:34,080
So my question to you is: why is STEM so hot right now,

213
00:11:34,080 --> 00:11:37,560
yet considered- quote- Cub stuff, unquote.

214
00:11:37,560 --> 00:11:39,040
Well, thanks for getting in touch

215
00:11:39,040 --> 00:11:40,840
and let me see if I can answer your question,

216
00:11:40,840 --> 00:11:44,480
because I'm- and I should take the opportunity to say here

217
00:11:44,480 --> 00:11:47,660
that I am- not a scouting official of any kind.

218
00:11:47,660 --> 00:11:49,000
I'm just a volunteer scouter.

219
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:51,800
so I don't speak for anyone other than myself,

220
00:11:51,800 --> 00:11:55,200
and it's been a while since I've been to a round table

221
00:11:55,200 --> 00:11:56,540
or a district or council event.

222
00:11:56,540 --> 00:11:58,400
so I really don't have a handle

223
00:11:58,400 --> 00:12:01,280
on what people are saying about STEM.

224
00:12:01,280 --> 00:12:03,280
I don't know if it's hot or cold,

225
00:12:03,280 --> 00:12:05,000
I don't know why it's being characterized

226
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:07,040
as something just for Cub scouts.

227
00:12:07,040 --> 00:12:10,320
All I know is what I've seen about the program

228
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:12,960
and what I've concluded about it myself.

229
00:12:12,960 --> 00:12:16,400
So I'm happy to hear that you, as a Wolf Den leader,

230
00:12:16,400 --> 00:12:18,200
are particularly motivated about STEM

231
00:12:18,200 --> 00:12:20,320
and it has a connection to your profession.

232
00:12:20,320 --> 00:12:21,840
I think that's great

233
00:12:21,840 --> 00:12:23,800
and I'm glad that you've been working

234
00:12:23,800 --> 00:12:25,440
with successful programs

235
00:12:25,440 --> 00:12:27,560
and I'm sure that your Cubs

236
00:12:27,560 --> 00:12:29,800
