237
00:12:29,800 --> 00:12:34,720
My own take on STEM is: I don't see how it fits scouting.

238
00:12:34,720 --> 00:12:37,920
I see it as another attempt to try to lend relevance

239
00:12:37,920 --> 00:12:39,520
to scouting programs. perhaps

240
00:12:39,520 --> 00:12:42,160
from those who believe that sort of thing is needed.

241
00:12:42,160 --> 00:12:44,240
I don't particularly see the need.

242
00:12:44,240 --> 00:12:46,040
Now the scouts that I work with,

243
00:12:46,040 --> 00:12:48,520
the scouts in my troop, seem to be perfectly happy

244
00:12:48,520 --> 00:12:51,439
with. camping is the emphasis and center of the program.

245
00:12:51,439 --> 00:12:53,840
I don't think we have lost relevance

246
00:12:53,840 --> 00:12:55,640
or connection with our scouts

247
00:12:55,640 --> 00:12:57,319
and they don't seem to be missing

248
00:12:57,319 --> 00:12:59,439
the whole STEM thing at all.

249
00:12:59,439 --> 00:13:02,000
I know that they are interested in those merit badges

250
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:02,840
and they do them.

251
00:13:02,840 --> 00:13:05,680
We don't do merit badges as a part of the troop program

252
00:13:05,680 --> 00:13:08,760
and I know that they're interested in those subjects.

253
00:13:08,760 --> 00:13:12,040
but my simple take on scouting at any age level

254
00:13:12,040 --> 00:13:14,319
is that we develop character

255
00:13:14,319 --> 00:13:16,600
through the application of the patrol method

256
00:13:16,600 --> 00:13:19,280
and I see my work as a scouter providing opportunities

257
00:13:19,280 --> 00:13:21,360
for scouts to go camping with their friends

258
00:13:21,360 --> 00:13:24,280
and work the patrol method.

259
00:13:24,280 --> 00:13:26,120
I know it sounds simplistic

260
00:13:26,120 --> 00:13:28,400
and I'm sure in some ways, that it is,

261
00:13:28,400 --> 00:13:30,320
but there's an awful lot of complex things

262
00:13:30,320 --> 00:13:33,520
that go underneath the surface when you go camping

263
00:13:33,520 --> 00:13:36,600
and I've talked about them at great length in the past,

264
00:13:36,600 --> 00:13:39,000
so I won't go into it here

265
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:42,040
and I'm not trying to be negative.

266
00:13:42,040 --> 00:13:44,880
All I wanna say is: look,

267
00:13:44,920 --> 00:13:47,120
labs and classrooms and workshops

268
00:13:47,120 --> 00:13:48,439
are some of my favorite places.

269
00:13:48,439 --> 00:13:49,640
They have been all my life.

270
00:13:49,640 --> 00:13:52,120
I love learning new skills,

271
00:13:52,120 --> 00:13:54,240
I love learning how to work with things,

272
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:56,760
I love learning the science of things

273
00:13:56,760 --> 00:13:58,920
and I think that's a wonderful pursuit.

274
00:13:58,920 --> 00:14:03,280
I just don't see it as being particularly relevant

275
00:14:03,280 --> 00:14:05,439
to the focus of scouting.

276
00:14:05,439 --> 00:14:10,440
To my mind, it's as discordant as setting up a tent

277
00:14:10,580 --> 00:14:12,160
and going camping in a laboratory

278
00:14:12,160 --> 00:14:13,720
or workshop or a classroom.

279
00:14:13,720 --> 00:14:15,200
You know, I don't say that these two things

280
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:16,280
are totally divorced.

281
00:14:16,280 --> 00:14:20,200
I'm just saying the important word here is focus right,

282
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:22,320
Because there are plenty of STEM things

283
00:14:22,320 --> 00:14:24,540
that happen in the course of a camp out.

284
00:14:24,540 --> 00:14:27,280
There are plenty of STEM things that happen

285
00:14:27,280 --> 00:14:30,960
in the course of a scout advancing in rank.

286
00:14:30,960 --> 00:14:32,440
You know, look at the requirements,

287
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:34,180
look at the things that they have to do.

288
00:14:34,180 --> 00:14:35,960
These have to do with science,

289
00:14:35,960 --> 00:14:38,000
technology, engineering and mathematics.

290
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:40,840
I'm just saying I don't see a particular need

291
00:14:40,840 --> 00:14:43,800
to focus on those in isolation.

292
00:14:43,800 --> 00:14:47,440
I think they're a great part of the overall package.

293
00:14:47,440 --> 00:14:49,860
You know, the BSA has had many things,

294
00:14:49,860 --> 00:14:53,260
many kinds of programs like this that have been tried

295
00:14:53,260 --> 00:14:55,240
and they gain a lot of interest for a few years

296
00:14:55,240 --> 00:14:57,020
and then they kind of fade away.

297
00:14:57,020 --> 00:15:01,080
Maybe the whole STEM emphasis has a more staying power.

298
00:15:01,080 --> 00:15:02,800
I prefer to stick with what I see

299
00:15:02,800 --> 00:15:05,040
as best serving young people who become scouts,

300
00:15:05,040 --> 00:15:06,840
and that's working the patrol method

301
00:15:06,840 --> 00:15:10,320
and going camping and building character.

302
00:15:10,320 --> 00:15:13,000
and once again, I'm not being negative,

303
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:15,880
I'm just saying I don't see a whole lot of value

304
00:15:15,880 --> 00:15:18,400
in that particular focus.

305
00:15:18,400 --> 00:15:20,000
And, all that being said,

306
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:23,440
I'm always happy when I hear that scouts of any age

307
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:26,600
are happy themselves and engaged in learning,

308
00:15:26,600 --> 00:15:29,360
no matter what the program, no matter what the focus.

309
00:15:29,360 --> 00:15:31,280
This last email comes from Robert,

310
00:15:31,280 --> 00:15:33,700
who's a scout master in Massachusetts,

311
00:15:33,700 --> 00:15:36,440
and he says: I'm feeling a bit down. right now.

312
00:15:36,440 --> 00:15:38,440
The scouts in our troop are aging out

313
00:15:38,440 --> 00:15:41,720
and our recruiting effort is kind of falling flat.

314
00:15:41,720 --> 00:15:44,960
We are doing all we can to encourage weeblos

315
00:15:44,960 --> 00:15:49,040
who unfortunately keep choosing to go to a different troop.

316
00:15:49,040 --> 00:15:52,360
I'm starting to feel that the troop might be doomed.

317
00:15:52,360 --> 00:15:55,040
Oh, Robert, I know this feeling.

318
00:15:55,040 --> 00:15:59,880
I know the feeling because over the past 35,, 36 years

319
00:15:59,880 --> 00:16:04,000
as a scout master I've been through some very long

320
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:07,800
dry periods with recruiting weeblos.

321
00:16:07,800 --> 00:16:10,720
So I do know how this feels and it's not good.

322
00:16:10,720 --> 00:16:12,880
But before I give you any advice,

323
00:16:12,880 --> 00:16:16,560
I will tell you, as unsettling as it may sound,

324
00:16:16,560 --> 00:16:18,840
that units do have a lifespan.

325
00:16:18,840 --> 00:16:21,000
Troops and things like that do have a lifespan.

326
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:23,320
We used to have five troops in town

327
00:16:23,320 --> 00:16:25,600
and that dwindled down to two-

328
00:16:25,600 --> 00:16:28,140
almost one- for a couple years.

329
00:16:28,140 --> 00:16:29,840
Now we have three.

330
00:16:29,840 --> 00:16:32,160
The three troops are doing fine.

331
00:16:32,160 --> 00:16:35,940
They each have a slightly different way of doing business.

332
00:16:35,940 --> 00:16:38,340
The two troops that went away were around

333
00:16:38,340 --> 00:16:41,740
for years and years and years and things just happened

334
00:16:41,740 --> 00:16:44,620
And sometimes there's nothing that can be done about it.

335
00:16:44,620 --> 00:16:46,940
You know it's a complex mixture of problems

336
00:16:46,940 --> 00:16:51,260
and changes and logistics and sometimes units go away

337
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:54,180
And when that happens it's not likely it's because

338
00:16:54,180 --> 00:16:58,100
of one particular person's lack of effort

339
00:16:58,100 --> 00:17:01,060
or that a group of people have done something wrong

340
00:17:01,060 --> 00:17:02,660
or anything like that.

341
00:17:02,660 --> 00:17:05,660
Things just have a lifespan sometimes.

342
00:17:05,660 --> 00:17:08,140
Now I don't say that to discourage anyone,

343
00:17:08,140 --> 00:17:10,820
because I know you're gonna keep on doing all that you can

344
00:17:10,820 --> 00:17:12,420
for your troop.

345
00:17:12,420 --> 00:17:14,740
I say it because you aren't alone

346
00:17:14,740 --> 00:17:16,580
in your frustration with the situation

347
00:17:16,580 --> 00:17:19,060
and all likelihood it's not your fault.

348
00:17:19,060 --> 00:17:21,060
So just in case you're feeling a fault,

349
00:17:21,060 --> 00:17:22,900
don't put that on yourself.

350
00:17:22,900 --> 00:17:24,660
So here's my advice.

351
00:17:24,660 --> 00:17:27,180
I began to understand in one of these

352
00:17:27,180 --> 00:17:30,420
long, dry recruiting periods where all the weeblos

353
00:17:30,420 --> 00:17:32,860
everywhere seem to be joining over troops,

354
00:17:32,860 --> 00:17:34,860
that weeblos are not only

355
00:17:34,860 --> 00:17:37,780
or even the best source of new scouts.

356
00:17:37,780 --> 00:17:40,940
I mean, our informal analysis of new scouts

357
00:17:40,940 --> 00:17:44,620
and how long they last over the past seven to 10 years

358
00:17:44,620 --> 00:17:47,700
tells us that the weeblos that we have gotten

359
00:17:47,700 --> 00:17:49,420
are much more likely to drop out

360
00:17:49,420 --> 00:17:51,700
than the boys who've joined the troop,

361
00:17:51,700 --> 00:17:52,900
who were never scouts.

362
00:17:52,900 --> 00:17:57,340
So at one point we kind of stopped chasing weeblos,

363
00:17:57,340 --> 00:18:00,780
mostly because we weren't getting any-

364
00:18:00,780 --> 00:18:05,020
So it's not like we were getting droves of weeblos-

365
00:18:05,020 --> 00:18:06,660
and we said, no, let's stop this.

366
00:18:06,660 --> 00:18:08,700
We just said that's not going to be

367
00:18:08,700 --> 00:18:11,100
our only emphasis anymore.

368
00:18:11,100 --> 00:18:14,460
We scaled back our efforts in that wise

369
00:18:14,460 --> 00:18:18,020
and we upped our efforts in recruiting all the time

370
00:18:18,020 --> 00:18:21,260
from anybody who was interested in being a scout.

371
00:18:21,260 --> 00:18:23,899
Now we still have plenty of weeblos dens visit

372
00:18:23,899 --> 00:18:26,100
and we have some join now and again

373
00:18:26,100 --> 00:18:29,500
and I think we have three or four coming in this spring.

374
00:18:29,540 --> 00:18:31,060
but when weeblos come to visit

375
00:18:31,060 --> 00:18:32,980
we're very clear about the kind of troop we are

376
00:18:32,980 --> 00:18:34,740
and what our expectations are,

377
00:18:34,740 --> 00:18:36,980
and that there's another troop across town

378
00:18:36,980 --> 00:18:39,580
and you really should make sure to visit them

379
00:18:39,580 --> 00:18:41,180
and see what's going on there.

380
00:18:41,180 --> 00:18:43,660
We're interested in recruiting weeblos.

381
00:18:43,660 --> 00:18:45,900
We just don't put up a whole lot of fight.

382
00:18:45,900 --> 00:18:49,540
So that was kind of. step one was to say, okay,

383
00:18:49,540 --> 00:18:51,820
this is not the only way that you get new scouts.

384
00:18:51,820 --> 00:18:55,180
Step two was understanding that there are two,

385
00:18:55,180 --> 00:18:58,260
and only two, ways to recruit scouts

386
00:18:58,260 --> 00:19:01,300
that seem to work on a consistent basis,

387
00:19:01,300 --> 00:19:02,900
And I think I've talked about this before

388
00:19:02,900 --> 00:19:05,340
but, at the risk of repeating myself,

389
00:19:05,340 --> 00:19:07,180
here are the two ways.

390
00:19:07,180 --> 00:19:11,140
One, scouts talk to their friends who are of scout age.

391
00:19:11,140 --> 00:19:16,100
Two, parents of scouts talk to parents of scout aged boys.

392
00:19:16,100 --> 00:19:17,980
Those are the two ways that work.

393
00:19:17,980 --> 00:19:20,060
So, Robert, in your particular situation,

394
00:19:20,060 --> 00:19:21,500
here's what I would suggest you do:

395
00:19:21,500 --> 00:19:23,300
Get your scouts together

396
00:19:23,300 --> 00:19:24,780
and tell them their challenges

397
00:19:24,780 --> 00:19:28,100
to each identify at least five boys

398
00:19:28,100 --> 00:19:30,180
who they can invite to scouts.

399
00:19:30,180 --> 00:19:31,780
Get the families together.

400
00:19:31,780 --> 00:19:33,420
Tell parents you'd like them to talk

401
00:19:33,420 --> 00:19:34,940
to at least five other families

402
00:19:34,940 --> 00:19:37,460
about having their son join scouts.

403
00:19:37,460 --> 00:19:40,100
Now you and I both know that not every scout

404
00:19:40,100 --> 00:19:43,060
and not every parent is going to come through on this,

405
00:19:43,060 --> 00:19:46,020
but don't pay attention to who doesn't come through

406
00:19:46,020 --> 00:19:48,380
as much as paying attention to who does.

407
00:19:48,380 --> 00:19:49,380
Give them a goal.

408
00:19:49,380 --> 00:19:51,260
The parents need to find five,

409
00:19:51,260 --> 00:19:53,540
The scouts individually need to find five,

410
00:19:53,540 --> 00:19:56,740
And then give them a good call to action

411
00:19:56,740 --> 00:19:59,260
for those boys and parents that they talk to,

412
00:19:59,260 --> 00:20:02,460
and that is, invite them to go on a camping trip,

413
00:20:02,460 --> 00:20:05,460
Not to a meeting, necessarily, but a camping trip.

414
00:20:05,460 --> 00:20:08,260
And it's important to emphasize camping over meetings

415
00:20:08,260 --> 00:20:09,860
because, of course, if they want to go camping,

416
00:20:09,860 --> 00:20:11,340
they're going to have to make at least one meeting

417
00:20:11,340 --> 00:20:13,820
to find out what to bring in such.

418
00:20:13,820 --> 00:20:17,060
That's why I say emphasize camping. meetings will follow.

419
00:20:17,060 --> 00:20:19,820
Then make it as easy as possible

420
00:20:19,820 --> 00:20:22,340
for all these possible new recruits to go camping.

421
00:20:22,340 --> 00:20:23,500
They can be guests.

422
00:20:23,500 --> 00:20:24,860
They don't have to be registered.

423
00:20:24,900 --> 00:20:26,820
Just take them along with as little fuss

424
00:20:26,820 --> 00:20:28,460
and paperwork as possible.

425
00:20:28,460 --> 00:20:30,740
Don't even mention joining the troop.

426
00:20:30,740 --> 00:20:34,060
Wait until they or their parents ask how to join.

427
00:20:34,060 --> 00:20:37,180
I guarantee that the scouts and the parents of scouts

428
00:20:37,180 --> 00:20:40,380
will be talking to them about those particulars. anyway,

429
00:20:40,380 --> 00:20:44,460
I think our message as scouts is: come camping with us.

430
00:20:44,460 --> 00:20:46,100
We'd love to have you come as a guest

431
00:20:46,100 --> 00:20:48,460
and make that as simple as possible.

432
00:20:48,460 --> 00:20:50,900
I wouldn't try to have a big, special camping trip

433
00:20:50,900 --> 00:20:53,940
for visitors. just go camping like you usually do

434
00:20:53,940 --> 00:20:56,180
and make having visitors a habit,

435
00:20:56,180 --> 00:20:58,900
something that happens as often as possible.

436
00:20:58,900 --> 00:21:00,180
See if you can get a visitor

437
00:21:00,180 --> 00:21:02,260
for every single trip you go on.

438
00:21:02,260 --> 00:21:04,580
Don't play too close attention to them.

439
00:21:04,580 --> 00:21:06,860
Let them do what your scouts do

440
00:21:06,860 --> 00:21:08,500
And I'll bet you'll have some new scouts

441
00:21:08,500 --> 00:21:09,780
in pretty short order.

442
00:21:09,780 --> 00:21:12,420
That's a pretty simple approach

443
00:21:12,420 --> 00:21:16,340
And it's one that I know works.

444
00:21:16,340 --> 00:21:18,700
I've tried just about everything else:

445
00:21:18,700 --> 00:21:22,420
Special meetings, special trips, flyers,

446
00:21:22,420 --> 00:21:26,980
things in the school newsletter, school visits,

447
00:21:26,980 --> 00:21:30,820
putting up signs advertising.

448
00:21:30,820 --> 00:21:35,820
none of that has netted us one single new scout.

449
00:21:36,100 --> 00:21:38,780
But I can say pretty reliably:

450
00:21:38,780 --> 00:21:43,340
if a boy who is not a scout goes camping with us,

451
00:21:43,340 --> 00:21:48,220
they will join the next week about 9.9 out of 10 times.

452
00:21:48,220 --> 00:21:49,660
So, Robert, I hope that helps.

453
00:21:49,660 --> 00:21:51,260
Again, it's not your fault.

454
00:21:51,260 --> 00:21:54,820
Sometimes these things have lifespans and things change,

455
00:21:54,820 --> 00:21:59,820
but I hope those ideas will gain some traction

456
00:21:59,940 --> 00:22:01,700
and make a difference for you.

457
00:22:01,700 --> 00:22:02,820
Hey, I'd love to hear from you

458
00:22:02,820 --> 00:22:05,260
if you have a question or a comment,

459
00:22:05,260 --> 00:22:07,300
and I'm pretty easy to get in touch with.

460
00:22:07,300 --> 00:22:09,260
I'm gonna tell you how to do that in just a moment.

461
00:22:09,260 --> 00:22:13,260
["Band Warms Up with You"].

462
